@prefix chorus: <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# #3675 — first chorus:Service instance (the /services collection was count:0 for
# every product). Pattern mirrors product-instances.ttl (#3603): this file is the
# DEFINITION home (ServiceShape floor content); structural edges (hosts / atStep)
# live in roles/silas/ontology/chorus.ttl. This file is in chorus-model-deploy's
# MODEL_SET from day one — never live-only (the #3587/#3593 lesson).
# IRI grammar follows product-clearing: chorus:service-<name>.
# FK targets verified live 2026-07-23: chorus:wren (AgentRole ⊑ Role),
# chorus:messages (Domain), chorus:value-stream-step-directing
# (ValueStreamStep — NOTE: lives in urn:chorus:instances, cross-graph; Silas
# review point #1).

chorus:service-clearing a chorus:Service ;
    chorus:oidcClientId "https://clearing.lightlifeurbangardens.com/clientid.jsonld" ;   # #4412
    rdfs:label "The Clearing service" ; chorus:label "The Clearing service" ;
    chorus:overview "Browser-based multi-party chat where Jeff and the three agent roles align in real time. Serves the room at :3470 (com.chorus.clearing) and a public door at clearing.lightlifeurbangardens.com via Cloudflare tunnel. Messages persist to the messaging store, transcripts index into the Chorus memory, DECISION: lines are captured to the decision log, and outbound delivery to agent sessions rides pulse through the session registry (tty, vscode, and tmux pane-first transports)." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-wren ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live and proven end-to-end 2026-07-23: phone to clearing.lightlifeurbangardens.com to a locked-screen wren session over the tmux pane transport (#3668). WebSocket bridge token now enforced on tunneled traffic (#3669 lane 1). Remaining as-is gaps: the public door has no per-participant authentication (any holder of the URL reaches the room), share.* export is unreliable, and delivery to agents is terminal injection rather than subscription." ;
    chorus:toBe "Every participant, human or agent, authenticates through the identity seam (#3613): agents via client-credentials with DPoP, humans via browser OIDC, verified against the seam's JWKS. Delivery moves toward agents subscribing to a signed log rather than terminal injection - substrate decision pending the Buzz spike (#3674, adopt / steal-the-pattern / pass). The service-design page regenerates from this model instead of being hand-maintained HTML." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "Sequence: (1) #3669 lanes 2-3 with Silas - replace the static bridge token with Solid-OIDC via the seam; the tunnel breaks DPoP htu unless the verifier reconstructs the external URL, and going public removes the loopback bound that let the seam skip DPoP. (2) #3674 spike readout decides the substrate (self-hosted Nostr relay vs current bespoke path). (3) Regenerate designing/docs/clearing-service-design.html from this instance and retire the hand-authored April version." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when the public door requires seam-issued identity for every participant, the substrate decision from #3674 is recorded on this instance, and the service-design page is generated from the graph with the April hand-authored page retired." ;
    chorus:gaps "Public door has no per-participant authentication - any holder of the URL reaches the room (#3669 lanes 2-3). share.* export is unreliable. Delivery to agents is terminal injection, not subscription (#3674 decides the substrate). The service-design HTML page is still hand-authored, not generated from this instance. hasDesignDoc unfilled - no Document instances exist in the graph." ;
    chorus:notInScope "Nudge transport and session-registry routing (pulse owns delivery; the Clearing hands outbound messages to pulse). Spine event persistence (Spine product). Card and board mutations (werk / cards). Voice input (/listen). Substrate replacement itself - #3674 is a spike commitment to a readout, not to adoption." .
@prefix chorus: <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# #3870 — Service ONE of nine: Identity. Pair-review copy (kade drafts, wren
# navigates, silas gates — authN is his domain per Jeff's 2026-07-24 cut).
# BOUNDARY (issuance-only — wren's red-line 16:04 applied): a running thing
# is INSIDE Identity iff it MINTS who-you-are — issues tokens, holds signing
# keys, publishes JWKS, owns WebIDs. VERIFICATION IS A LIBRARY consumers
# embed: the verify code runs inside chorus-api, the app, the clearing — those
# instances deploy to THEIR Services, not to Identity. Two people agree at
# instance level: does this process mint identity? CSS pod: yes, inside — and
# it is Identity's ONLY instance (com.security.css). chorus-api verifying a
# token: outside. authorized-users.ts deciding access: outside (authZ).

chorus:service-identity a chorus:Service ;
    chorus:oidcClientId "https://chorus.lightlifeurbangardens.com/_auth/clientid.jsonld" ;   # #4412 — the shared sign-in page
    rdfs:label "Identity" ; chorus:label "Identity" ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-silas ;
    chorus:status "building" ;
    # #4503 — the design, in ADR-029's order, in the graph (Jeff 2026-10-12: "only 1 login /
    # sign in flow", "its for chorus not a page", "accidental architecture"). overview is §2.
    chorus:overview """You sign in to Chorus once, as yourself, and every Chorus surface knows who you are without asking again. An agent proves who it is the same way every time, and no one, person or agent, can act as someone else. Identity answers only who; what that principal may do is the roles domain's answer.""" ;
    chorus:contract """Person's browser to the door: GET /_auth/login, the identity provider, then /_auth/callback. Returns a signed session cookie for .lightlifeurbangardens.com naming the WebID, the Session row (sid) and when it was signed in. Fails: identity-provider-down, no-webid. Side effect: one open Session row for this browser; a sign-in that carries the browser's earlier cookie closes that row first.""" , """Every Chorus surface (pages behind the door, the Clearing, the app) to the door: GET /_auth/whoami with the cookie returns 200 {webid, allowed} or 401; GET /_auth/renew returns 204 with a renewed cookie or 401. Fails: anonymous, logged-out, expired, not-authorized. Side effect: on renew, the Session's lastSeenAt and expiresAt move. No surface keeps a sign-in or a session of its own.""" , """Person to the door: GET /_auth/logout. Clears the cookie at the scope it was set and closes the Session row. Every surface reads the person as signed out on its next request. The only sign-out.""" , """Agent (chorus-principal login <role>) to the identity provider: a client-credentials grant from the agent's own account returns a token naming its WebID. The agent then writes its own Session, SessionRun and Presence through the model door. Fails: identity-provider-down, not-owner (403 on any row it does not own).""" , """Any API door (athena-make, chorus-api) to chorus-oidc: verify a bearer token against the provider's keys and resolve its Principal. Returns the principal, or 401 invalid-token. Writes are then judged on the row's owner: 403 not-owner, 403 deploy-only for Principal rows.""" ;
    chorus:contract """chorus-api's roles view (the Clearing tile) to the model door: GET /v1/identity/sessions and /v1/identity/presences, read-only. Returns each principal's open sessions; a person shows one per browser. Fails: unavailable (the store did not answer), never an empty list in its place. No side effect.""" ,
        """chorus-principal (login <role>, the agent half of identity) to the model door: reads the person's open browser Session before starting a role in his name (#4412). Returns the open Session, or refuses the start when there is none: no-person-session. Side effect: none on his row; the agent writes only its own rows.""" ;
    chorus:validation """The door validates on every request before anything is proxied or written: the cookie's signature, its expiry (12 hours idle), its sign-in time (30 days at most), and that its Session row is still open. API doors verify a bearer token before any write. A failed check returns its named state (anonymous, logged-out, expired, not-authorized) as a 401 or 403 and never proxies, writes or renews.""" ;
    chorus:failureMode """identity-provider-down: the sign-in page says identity is down; never a generic error.""" , """anonymous: no valid cookie. A browser gets the sign-in page, a script gets 401.""" , """logged-out: the cookie names a Session that was signed out. Fails on its next request, however recently used.""" , """expired: idle past 12 hours, or past 30 days since sign-in however recently used.""" , """not-authorized: signed in, not in the allow-set for this surface (403).""" , """not-owner: a write to a Session, SessionRun or Presence row another principal owns (403). No Permission row opens it.""" , """deploy-only: a session tried to create or change a Principal. Who exists is written by the model deploy only (403).""" ;
    chorus:asIs """Measured 2026-10-12: three sign-ins (the door; the Clearing's own /auth/login, /auth/callback and /auth/signout; the app's /login form on :3000), so Jeff held 5 open sessions at once, 2 of them 30-day Clearing sign-ins. 15 agent and service WebIDs are pods of Jeff's identity-provider account (seed-css.sh), so his sign-in page offers a picker of 12 and a person can sign in as a role. The door renews on use and replaces a same-browser sign-in (#4500). No role holds a grant on the identity graph, so each writes only its own rows (#4204).""" ;
    chorus:toBe """One door. Every Chorus surface trusts it and none signs in or out by itself, the home network included. One browser holds one session. Each agent and service has its own identity-provider account, so a person's sign-in names only that person and shows no picker.""" ;
    chorus:implementationPlan """A (#4412 reopen, Wren for the Clearing, Kade for the app): delete the Clearing's /auth/login, /auth/callback, its own Session writes and its sign-out, and the app's /login form; both ask the door. B (#4503, Silas): a check that two sign-ins from one browser leave one open row, and Jeff's tile shows one session per browser. A and B land together. C (#4503, Silas): move each agent and service WebID to its own account, keeping its IRI: new account, link the WebID, new client credential, swap identity/<name>/cred.json, check its login, then unlink it from Jeff's account. zzz-test first (unlink only), then the services, then each role.""" ;
    chorus:filesInScope "platform/scripts/chorus-share-guard.py" , "platform/scripts/lib/person_session.py" ,
        "platform/services/chorus-principal" , "platform/services/chorus-oidc" , "platform/scripts/seed-css.sh" ,
        "directing/clearing/src/server.ts" , "directing/clearing/src/person-session.ts" ,
        "jeff-bridwell-personal-site (the app's /login)" ;
    chorus:reference """ADR-029: every service design follows the template, consumers before providers.""" ,
        """ADR-048 §3: field exposure tiers; #4503 makes every design section public, since the door already signs a reader in.""" ,
        """#4204: no Permission row opens the identity graph; each principal writes only its own rows.""" ,
        """#4220: Principal is deploy-only; who exists is not session-writable.""" ,
        """#4383: each principal runs as its own Mac account.""" ,
        """#4412: login is bound to the person's live browser session; the Clearing half of one sign-in (A).""" ,
        """#4500: the door renews a session on use (12 hours idle, 30 days at most) and replaces a same-browser sign-in.""" ,
        """#4503: one sign-in to Chorus, one session per browser, each principal its own account.""" ,
        """no-app-owns-the-door (2026-08-08): no product holds the sign-in decision.""" ;
    chorus:pathToClose """Closed when Jeff signs in once with no picker, every Chorus surface trusts that sign-in, his tile shows one session per browser, and no WebID but his can be chosen from his account.""" ;
    chorus:gaps """The identity provider is a single instance, a hard-fail dependency for every login. The door and person_session.py are scripts, not code units, so blast radius cannot see a sign-in change. The Host-spoof the app's old login needed is unverified since August.""" ;
    chorus:notInScope """Authorization of any kind: allow-sets, role grants, per-surface permissions (roles domain). Nostr key derivation for Buzz.""" ;
    chorus:diagram """%% As is: three doors (measured 2026-10-12)
flowchart LR
  browser[Person's browser] -->|sign in| door[The door]
  browser -->|its own sign-in| clearing[Clearing]
  browser -->|its own /login| app[Gathering app]
  door -->|OIDC| idp[Identity provider]
  clearing -->|OIDC| idp
  door -->|Session rows| make[Model door]
  clearing -->|Session rows| make
  idp -->|15 WebIDs on Jeff's account| browser""" , """%% To be: one door
flowchart LR
  browser[Person's browser] -->|sign in / sign out| door[The door]
  door -->|OIDC, his WebID only| idp[Identity provider]
  door -->|one Session per browser| make[Model door]
  clearing[Clearing] -->|whoami / renew| door
  app[Gathering app] -->|whoami| door
  agent[chorus-principal] -->|own account, client credentials| idp
  agent -->|own Session rows| make""" ,
        """%% Consumers: who calls identity (ADR-029 consumer diagram)
flowchart LR
  browser[Person's browser] -->|sign in / sign out| door[The door]
  door -->|OIDC| idp[Identity provider]
  clearing[Clearing] -->|whoami / renew| door
  app[Gathering app] -->|whoami| door
  pages[Pages behind the door] -->|proxied after whoami| door
  agent[chorus-principal] -->|client credentials| idp
  agent -->|own Session rows| make[Model door]
  make -->|verify bearer| oidc[chorus-oidc]""" , """%% Sign-in, the critical path (ADR-029 sequence)
sequenceDiagram
  participant B as Browser
  participant D as The door
  participant P as Identity provider
  participant M as Model door
  B->>D: GET /_auth/login
  D->>P: authorize (his WebID only)
  P-->>D: code
  D->>P: token
  alt provider down
    D-->>B: identity is down
  else ok
    D->>M: close this browser's old Session, open one
    D-->>B: Set-Cookie (webid, sid, iat)
  end
  B->>D: any page, cookie
  D->>D: verify signature, expiry, sid open
  alt logged-out or expired
    D-->>B: sign-in page (401)
  else ok
    D-->>B: page, renewed cookie
  end""" .

# Instances observed (from instances-observed.json; the harvester will own
# these rows in the graph — listed here only as the deploys-mapping spec):
#   instance-library-com.gathering.blockverse? NO — outside (app).
#   CSS pod runs as... (launchd label verified below in pair review)
#   deploys→ chorus:service-identity: the CSS pod unit on library.

# #3870 — Service: Loom. Jeff's cut 2026-08-14 ~09:34: coordination splits
# Clearing (delivery to screens) / Loom (watching and guarding role turns).
# BOUNDARY (two-people-agree): INSIDE Loom iff its subject is ROLE TURNS —
# observing, guarding, digesting them. hooks daemon: inside. pulse (delivers
# to screens): Clearing. chorus-api hosts loom endpoints among many: its
# instance deploys to several Services, loom included (shared-instance rule).
chorus:service-loom a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Loom" ; chorus:label "Loom" ;
    chorus:overview "The role-thread runtime — every tool turn a role takes passes through it. The chorus-hooks daemon guards each turn (canonical write guard, TDD gate, search hierarchy, respond-first), digests it for the streams, and emits the observation record peers and Jeff watch. Loom is why a role's work is visible and bounded at all." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-wren ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live: the daemon runs on a unix socket (no TCP), fail-closed for every role when down — the highest-blast-radius edge on the topology map (one restart command recovers). Observer digests cover shell/edit/agent/skill turns; MCP verbs digest to nothing (#3884). Gates fire per-turn with per-role config." ;
    chorus:toBe "Every tool class digests (#3884 kills the silent-empty default); pipeline phases interleave into streams so out-of-session work reads as work; daemon degradation surfaces as a named identity rather than mysterious tool denials (the #2790 lockout class, made legible)." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) #3884 digest-all + werk-phase interleave — carded, kade. (2) Daemon-down legibility: deny message names the daemon and the recovery line (exists; keep under test). (3) Tile cross-role lastAction misattribution seen once 2026-08-14 — reproduce with a fixture or retire the suspicion." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when no tool class is silently invisible, pipeline activity renders in streams, and a daemon outage names itself." ;
    chorus:gaps "MCP verbs invisible in streams (#3884, carded). Werk runs render as watcher sleeps. Possible tile misattribution (one observation, unconfirmed). hasDesignDoc unfilled pending Document instances (Silas review point 3)." ;
    chorus:notInScope "Message delivery to screens (Clearing/pulse). Card and board state (werk/cards). Gate POLICY content — loom runs gates; what they enforce belongs to the owning domains." .

# #3870 — Services four through nine, authored from Jeff's product cuts
# (2026-08-14: Knowledge Store = chorus context+memory+knowledge; Model
# Surface = Athena; "we are missing werk"; observability+security = borg;
# bedroom media/ai = gathering core; nifi = convergence 100%). Each carries
# the same two-people-agree boundary test the first three set. Structural
# edges live in roles/silas/ontology/chorus.ttl (Silas gate-arch).

chorus:service-athena a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Athena" ; chorus:label "Athena" ;
    chorus:overview "The model surface — the governed pen and the read door for the OWL model. owl-api on :3360 serves DECLARED-and-claimed classes as REST collections (/products, /services, /domains…); chorus-model is the DAL that refuses hand-typed IRIs and ungoverned writes; athena pages render domain detail from the graph. INSIDE iff its subject is the MODEL: serving it, mutating it under governance, rendering it. The store that persists triples is the Knowledge Store's, not Athena's." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-wren ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live: owl-api serves exactly definesVocabulary-claimed classes (DECLARED ⊃ CLAIMED ⊃ SERVED, lib.rs:863); the DAL + athena-model-gate close the back door; /services serves the three Services authored this week. Gap proven this card: /serviceinstances does not exist yet — harvested runtime rows have no read door." ;
    chorus:toBe "Every domain's collections regenerate from the model on land (#3551 direction); /serviceinstances serves the harvested graph; #3896 adds athena step instances with implementedBy + negativeFixture edges so pipeline gates are model-visible." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) Claim ServiceInstance/ScheduledJob vocabulary so owl-api mounts /serviceinstances (this card, with Silas's shape review). (2) #3896 (Silas) lands the athena step shape. (3) Topology page reads /services + /serviceinstances instead of a hand-list." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when the runtime registry is served from the graph and the topology page renders from it with zero hand-maintained service lists." ;
    chorus:gaps "/serviceinstances unmounted (vocabulary unclaimed). hasDesignDoc unfilled pending Document instances (Silas review point 3)." ;
    chorus:notInScope "Triple persistence (Knowledge Store). Pipeline execution (Werk). Page hosting for non-model pages (Gathering App / Clearing)." .

chorus:service-knowledge-store a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Knowledge Store" ; chorus:label "Knowledge Store" ;
    chorus:overview "Context, memory, and knowledge — Jeff's cut: 'Knowledge Store is really chorus.' The Fuseki triple store (:3030, 62GB shared store) is the persistence heart; chorus-api (:3340) is the read/write door for search, context injection, seeds, and cards views; the index/embedding workers keep FTS and vectors fresh; the crawler and context caches keep session boot cheap. INSIDE iff its subject is STORED KNOWLEDGE — persisting it, indexing it, retrieving it." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-wren ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live and load-bearing for every session boot (context inject) and every /chorus search. Known hard truths: one Fuseki instance on one machine serves both products; the 1.1GB FTS index once blocked the event loop (#3086 moved it off-loop); anonymous LAN writes remain possible pending the Shiro/DAL work (#3564 lineage)." ;
    chorus:toBe "Store writes go through governed doors only (DAL for model graphs, harvest loaders for runtime graphs, fuseki-auth everywhere); replies delivered over Buzz index into search automatically (#3893 Wren leg); backup/compact jobs stay boring and observable." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) #3893's search fan-out lands with Wren's subscriber. (2) Write-governance follow-through per the security substrate work (#3726 lineage). (3) Keep compact/backup under observability's watch rather than silent cron." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when every write surface is a governed door and reply/search freshness is proven by the delivery canary." ;
    chorus:gaps "Anonymous LAN write path still open at the store level. Single instance, single machine. hasDesignDoc unfilled." ;
    chorus:notInScope "Model governance semantics (Athena). Message delivery (Clearing/Buzz). Dashboards over the data (Observability)." .

chorus:service-werk a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Werk" ; chorus:label "Werk" ;
    chorus:overview "The pipeline that moves code from card to canonical — Jeff's cut: 'we are missing werk.' The Rust verb crates (werk-pull … werk-accept) are the state-transition gates; chorus-mcp (:3350) is the door roles invoke them through; act runs werk.yml as the one pipeline config; the board (vikunja) holds the cards the pipeline serves. INSIDE iff its subject is a STATE TRANSITION of work: pull, commit, test, demo, merge, accept." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-kade ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live: one trigger (chorus_werk), seven verbs, ephemeral per-card worktrees, blocking test floor (#3190), two-tier merge proof, DEC-048 accept authority, werk.phase events rendering in Jeff's streams since today (#3884). Hard truths from this week: a run pin can claim landed while unmerged (caught by the integrity refusal), and run state still lives in pins + spine rather than the graph." ;
    chorus:toBe "Pipelines and runs are model instances (the Pipeline domain sketch with Silas): typed steps with implementedBy + negativeFixture edges, runs with per-step metadata, pulse holding open runs as live state — loop position queryable, not archaeological." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) #3896 (Silas) lands the step shape; werk-* steps follow. (2) Run metadata projection from spine to graph. (3) Pulse renders open runs (the loop-state surface from Jeff's 2026-08-15 framing)." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when a run's position is a query, not a log grep, and every gate the pipeline enforces is declared with its negative fixture." ;
    chorus:gaps "Run state not in the graph. Landed-but-unmerged contradiction still possible at pin level (refused on read, not prevented at write). hasDesignDoc unfilled." ;
    chorus:notInScope "What the code does once deployed (each service owns its runtime). Card content authoring (roles). Model mutations (Athena)." ;
    chorus:consumesEvent chorus:eventtype-card-pulled .

chorus:service-tests a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Tests" ; chorus:label "Tests" ;
    chorus:overview "The service that answers 'is it tested, and did it pass' for every card and every night: the registry of tests (the tests domain, one row per test with layer, concern, hermeticity, covers), the runner that selects from that registry and executes it (werk-test: the blocking floor of every land and the whole-registry nightly), the evidence it stores (one TestResult per case), and the surfaces that read the evidence (the readout to Jeff, /nightly, the census). INSIDE iff its subject is a test's identity, selection, execution, evidence or readout." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-kade ;
    # Jeff, 2026-09-03 11:44: "isnt it building" — the test step is part of Building; the demo is Proving
    # #4093 — the flows, as data (chorus:diagram, Wren's #4094: repeatable mermaid, %% caption first line)
    chorus:diagram """%% As is (2026-09-03): the runner as it runs — a bash wrapper around the Rust binary, a python hydrator writing the registry
flowchart LR
  H[test file headers] --> HY[hydrator, every 15 min]
  HY --> REG[(registry graph)]
  REG --> WT[werk-test]
  NS[nightly wrapper, 03:00] --> WT
  CARD[card diff] --> WT
  WT --> L1[cargo] & L2[jest] & L3[node test] & L4[bats] & L5[shell] & L6[ui]
  L1 & L2 & L3 & L4 & L5 & L6 --> WB[write-back]
  WB --> LED[(results ledger)]
  LED --> RO[readout: page, nudge, census]
  NS -. coverage, shell, census legs .-> RO""" ;
    chorus:diagram """%% To be: one binary — the nightly is the same runner with selection = everything; wrapper and hydrator folded in; every registered test has a lane; the census reads zero
flowchart LR
  H[test file headers] --> WT[werk-test: registry, lanes, evidence, readout]
  CARD[card diff] --> WT
  ALL[selection = everything, 03:00] --> WT
  WT --> LED[(results ledger)]
  LED --> RO[readout in Jeff's tree: card, domain, kind]
  LED --> CEN[census = 0]""" ;
    chorus:status "building" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live: registry hydrated every 15 min from @test-type headers (7,808 tests); werk-test blocks every land and runs the 03:00 nightly (327 units, ~55 min); per-case results store under the nightly principal (#3975) and a run that loses its evidence fails (#4015); every red is labelled product-broke / test-wrong / unmeasured and delivered to Jeff after each run (#4060, #4073). Hard truths on 2026-09-03: the nightly still runs through a bash wrapper around the Rust runner and every red fixed that day sat on that seam (#4063); 149 registered tests never store a result, 112 of them in files no lane runs; the design of record was an unread HTML draft for eleven weeks." ;
    chorus:toBe "One binary: the nightly is the same runner every land uses with selection = everything, the bash legs and the python hydrator gone (#4017); the runner reports in Jeff's tree (card → domain → unit / page / integration / security), not by tool; every registered test has a lane and every executed case joins its registered identity, so the census reads zero; a red keeps its own evidence." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) #4089: this design as Commitment rows (retired 2026-10-01, #4064: a promise is a test on the service, not a row). (2) #4008 + #4014: runs cannot overlap, bats assertions can fail. (3) #4017: fold the five bash legs into werk-test, retire nightly-suites.sh. (4) #4007: the run narrates itself. (5) #3983: per-card test evidence at accept. (6) the selection gaps and the domain-shaped report, carded from the open commitments." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when the census is zero after a full run and Jeff reads the run in his own tree." ;
    chorus:gaps "112 registered files no lane runs (shell outside platform/scripts, sexuality-player js, cucumber features, playwright flows, python). TestResult keeps no role, trace or duration. The value axis (valid / asserts-retired-behavior / passes-by-definition) is not a governed property. Coverage and census output discarded on fail. hasDesignDoc unfilled: the design IS the commitment rows." ;
    chorus:notInScope "The toolchains themselves (jest, cargo, bats stay). Coverage floors and lint ratchets (werk-code gates that consume the same selection). Auto-registering tests the census finds (surfacing, never spawning)." .

chorus:service-gathering-app a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Gathering App" ; chorus:label "Gathering App" ;
    chorus:overview "Jeff's personal-infrastructure product as experienced in the browser — the Express app on :3000 with photos, music, property, garden, self — plus the bedroom media/AI cluster Jeff placed inside it: images-api (server + video), ollama (LLM inference), navidrome (music streaming), the self-ai player experiences. INSIDE iff Jeff experiences it as Gathering content or the compute that serves that content." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-kade ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live on library (app, blockverse, edge, mysql, wordpress) with the media/AI cluster on bedroom over NFS + SSH ops (DEC-089). CI green as of #3856. Bedroom units were invisible to the first harvester passes — three plist dirs + full-argv evidence fixed that in this card." ;
    chorus:toBe "Demo env can stand up the app's true dependency set because this registry names it; bedroom units carry the same lastObserved freshness as library's; media pipelines log to Loki like everything else." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) This card's harvester LaunchAgents on both machines keep the registry fresh. (2) Map remaining bedroom units as they're understood (volume-keepalive, sexuality-player mapped; toolkit/GoogleUpdater stay external). (3) Feed the demo-env dependency list from /serviceinstances." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when the app's full runtime dependency set is readable from the registry and the demo env consumes it." ;
    chorus:gaps "Bedroom freshness depends on SSH reachability. hasDesignDoc unfilled." ;
    chorus:notInScope "Coordination surfaces (Clearing). The store itself (Knowledge Store). Observability agents on the same boxes." .

chorus:service-observability a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Observability" ; chorus:label "Observability" ;
    chorus:overview "Borg's seeing half — Jeff's cut: 'observability and security are borg.' Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, promtail on both machines; alertmanager + the alert-notifier/runner delivery chain; the probe fleet (deep-health, chorus-health, bedroom-health, heartbeat, eventloop, clearing-probe, blackbox) and the exporters (node, mysqld, launchagent-metrics, harvest-exporter, nifi-metrics). INSIDE iff its subject is WATCHING other services and saying so — metrics, logs, probes, alerts." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-silas ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "Live across both machines; Loki is the durable log superset (tailing files is ephemeral); the probe fleet's recurring false-fire classes were each diagnosed 2026-07-10 — fragile probes, not outages. Hard truth: 26 standing warnings on the health surface reads as noise, and a broken monitor is a real defect to fix or retire, not weather." ;
    chorus:toBe "Zero-red nightly stays the bar; every probe that fires names a real state; run/loop positions join the watched surface via pulse (the loop-state work), so 'is it turning' is observable for pipelines the way 'is it up' is for services." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) Nightly triage discipline continues (#3890 lineage). (2) Warning-count burn-down owned by Silas. (3) Pulse run-state feed lands with the Pipeline domain." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when the standing-warning count is a worked queue, not a backdrop, and loop state is a first-class watched surface." ;
    chorus:gaps "26 standing warnings. Probe fleet still contains known-fragile members. hasDesignDoc unfilled." ;
    chorus:notInScope "Fixing what it observes (owning services). Identity/authN (Identity). The spine's persistence (Knowledge Store)." .

chorus:service-integration a chorus:Service ;
    rdfs:label "Integration" ; chorus:label "Integration" ;
    chorus:overview "Convergence's moving belt — Jeff's cut: 'nifi is convergence 100%.' Apache NiFi on bedroom carries bulk data flows between sources and the Gathering store; the harvest/ICD discipline (no harvester without a provider contract) governs what may flow. INSIDE iff its subject is MOVING data between systems under contract — flows, harvesters, ingestion." ;
    chorus:ownedBy chorus:principal-kade ;
    chorus:status "operating" ;
    chorus:asIs "NiFi live on bedroom (com.apache.nifi, with nifi-metrics exporting to observability). ICD gate enforces provider-before-harvester at edit time. Jeff's open framing: possibly a shared-integration project alongside shared-security and shared-observability." ;
    chorus:toBe "Flows declared as data with contracts (ICD instances) the same way pipelines declare steps; a flow's freshness and volume visible in observability; the shared-integration project decision recorded." ;
    chorus:implementationPlan "(1) Inventory NiFi flows against ICD providers. (2) Decide shared-integration placement with Jeff. (3) Wire flow metrics into the standard dashboards." ;
    chorus:pathToClose "Closed when every active flow maps to an ICD provider and the placement decision is recorded." ;
    chorus:gaps "Flow inventory not yet mapped to ICDs. Placement decision open. hasDesignDoc unfilled." ;
    chorus:notInScope "Store persistence (Knowledge Store). App-side rendering of converged data (Gathering App). One-shot scripts that aren't contracted flows." .
# #4503 — ADR-029 §3: the services that sign people in through, or verify principals with, identity.
chorus:service-clearing chorus:dependsOn chorus:service-identity .
chorus:service-gathering-app chorus:dependsOn chorus:service-identity .
chorus:service-athena chorus:dependsOn chorus:service-identity .
chorus:service-knowledge-store chorus:dependsOn chorus:service-identity .
